PASS / ADAPTER HARDENED / PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT PARTIAL

IMPLEMENTED
- External Agent Protocol v1.0 and the Pong Core schema remain unchanged.
- Default binding remains loopback; remote binding requires explicit opt-in.
- Request and response sizes are configurable and bounded.
- Protocol handlers use a configurable fixed worker count (default 8).
- A process-local per-principal fixed-window rate limiter protects admitted
  authenticated traffic and intentionally resets on process restart.
- Protocol-handler panics are caught, counted, and isolated from later clients.
- Runtime counters and a bounded 64-entry correlation snapshot cover request,
  Operation, Principal, Agent, Execution, Workspace, status, and latency.
- Opaque credentials are indexed by SHA-256 digest and never enter Pong Core.
- Credential replacement validates first and swaps atomically. New requests see
  rotation or revocation immediately; admitted requests and durable work are not
  cancelled or rewritten.
- The credential file must be a regular non-symlink no larger than 1 MiB. Unix
  group/other permissions are rejected. Windows ACL enforcement is NOT_PROVEN.

DEPLOYMENT BOUNDARY
- Plain HTTP is LOCAL DEVELOPMENT / EXPLICITLY TRUSTED NETWORK ONLY.
- Production remote deployment REQUIRES EXTERNAL TLS TERMINATION.
- tiny_http 0.12 has an internal dynamically growing connection parser pool
  and no exposed socket read/idle deadline.
- Global connection count, parser queue bound, slow-header/body defense, and an
  end-to-end adapter deadline are NOT_PROVEN.
- Production ingress must enforce TLS, connection limits, bounded queues,
  header/body/idle timeouts, and request deadlines.

